"""Limiting-quantifier detector for layers.0.mlp.down_proj:5780.

The component goes strongly negative inside the phrase "at least": on "least" itself
(about -1.2), and on the quantity word after it, most strongly "at least one" (about -4.4),
then "at least once" and "at least two" (about -2.5 to -3.5). It is moderately negative on
the same kind of quantity word after other limiters, such as "no one", "only one",
"exactly two", "not all", "almost every" (about -0.5). Smaller effects: "on" after a
motion or activity verb ("go on", "went on", "played on") is positive (about +0.75),
and "for" after "responsible", "necessary", "important" or "waiting" is about -0.5.
Everything else is treated as 0.
