"""Opening notation, particularly the ${ used in interpolation or mathematics.

Assign large positive values to dollar-brace interpolation, smaller values to
other brace/bracket openings and punctuation starting quoted text. Reduce the
response to math arguments and newline-ending code blocks. Keep 256 characters
of document-local history to recognize math versus quoted-code contexts. Most
ordinary tokens receive zero; these rules do not model their lexical variation.
